  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Cutting a lens in transverse direction doubles their focal length i.e. $2 f$. Using the formula of equivalent focal length, $\\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{1}{f_{1}}+\\frac{1}{f_{2}}+\\frac{1}{f_{3}}+\\frac{1}{f_{4}}$\r\n\r\nWe get equivalent focal length as $f / 2$",
